    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. but when you say \"strongly debated,\" it feels a bit vague. if you look at the actual data from that period, wouldn't most economists agree that the primary outcome was the revitalization of market efficiency and GDP growth, and that the inequality stuff is just a secondary side effect? like, is there a real consensus that the growth wasn't the main success story?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
