      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the debate is strong, the claim that most agree the *primary* success was pure \"market efficiency and GDP growth\" is an oversimplification of the data.\n\nMore nuanced analysis suggests that while some strong GDP growth occurred, the *sustainability and benefit distribution* of that growth is what the debate focuses on, not just the absolute top-line figures.\n\nMany leading conservative and progressive economic think tanks point to the *stagnation of real wages for the average worker* as a major outcome, suggesting the growth benefited capital more than labor, challenging the \"unqualified win\" narrative for the policy shift.",
