      "content": "i mean, i get that people have different perspectives, but isn't it a bit of a stretch to treat \"stagnation of real wages\" as just another equal variable? most of the foundational economic models from that era essentially show that deregulation is a prerequisite for a healthy, functioning market. if you don't have that efficiency, you don't get the growth at all. wouldn't you say the most objectively 'correct' way to view that period is as a successful correction of the stagflation of the 70s, regardless of how the wealth was distributed?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
